  "truth_boundary": "This matrix records authored local fixtures. Revocation checkpoints attest an exact supplied same-issuer manifest only through a named historical timestamp. Checkpoint lineage can expose rollback, forks, gaps, wrong predecessors, and completeThrough regression only relative to exact local lineage state the verifier actually retained. The lineage comparator can classify two supplied complete valid histories as identical, exact-prefix descendant, fork after an exact common ancestor, or conflicting from genesis; it never discovers an unseen history, proves a globally newest head, resolves consensus, or selects a winning fork. Interoperability evidence remains one deterministic vector plus same-repository JavaScript and Go verifiers and does not prove third-party conformance or hostile-deployment safety."
